  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Response to Congolese Refugees in Burundi</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">On 9th December 2025, rebels from the Alliance of the Congo River/March 23 Movement (AFC/M23) from Kamanyola have been advancing rapidly in Uvira, a city on the Burundian border, strategically located in the South Kivu province in the eastern region of DRC. Their advance has already caused a mass exodus of civilians to Burundi. The rebels have now been in control of Uvira and are strengthening their position and securing the city&apos;s surroundings with an even greater presence to the south. We can therefore expect further population movements in the coming days from the DRC into Burundi to seek refuge.</narrative>
  </description>
